#N canvas 30 30 2500 1900 12;
#X text 20 20 State Probe -- Phase 8's Step 0 \, and it must be SELECTED FROM THE MENU rather than deploy-loaded. It answers S0-1 through S0-4 in one press of System -> Save \, and it deliberately touches nothing in Cut It: mother's save behaviour is mother's \, so a separate patch measures it without dirtying the instrument., f 58;
#X text 900 20 IT RECORDS ITSELF BECAUSE THERE IS NO CONSOLE. A menu-launched patch sends stdout to tty1 \, so every finding goes to /sdcard/phase8-probe.log and is read back over ssh afterwards. Same reasoning as u_err's persistent log and AP Probe's., f 58;
#X text 1780 20 HOW TO RUN. Select State Probe from the menu. Wait for STATE PROBE on the screen. Press System -> Save. The second line should read SAVESTATE HIT. Then System -> Save New. Everything else is read off the device afterwards., f 58;
#X obj 20 340 loadbang;
#X obj 20 390 del 1000;
#X obj 20 440 t b b;
#X msg 200 500 symbol STATE-PROBE;
#X obj 200 555 s screenLine1;
#X msg 20 500 BOOT probe-start;
#X obj 660 340 loadbang;
#X obj 660 390 f 2000;
#X obj 660 440 until;
#X obj 660 490 t b b;
#X obj 860 550 f;
#X obj 860 600 t f f;
#X obj 1020 660 + 1;
#X msg 660 665 1 36 100 480;
#X obj 660 730 text set \$0-big;
#X obj 1400 340 loadbang;
#X obj 1400 390 del 1500;
#X obj 1400 440 t b b;
#X msg 1580 500 write -c probe-relative.txt;
#X msg 1400 500 RELWRITE attempted;
#X obj 20 680 r knob1;
#X obj 20 730 change -1;
#X obj 20 780 spigot 1;
#X msg 20 830 KNOB1 \$1;
#X obj 250 680 loadbang;
#X obj 250 730 del 3000;
#X msg 250 780 0;
#X obj 420 940 list append;
#X obj 420 990 t l b;
#X obj 620 1045 text size \$0-log;
#X obj 420 1100 text set \$0-log;
#X obj 20 1220 r saveState;
#X obj 20 1270 t a a a a a;
#X msg 1240 1400 SAVESTATE-HIT \$1;
#X obj 1000 1400 realtime;
#X msg 640 1400 write -c /tmp/state/probe-2000.txt;
#X msg 1000 1470 MS-2000 \$1;
#X obj 20 1340 t b b b;
#X msg 380 1410 write -c /tmp/state/probe-small.txt;
#X msg 200 1470 symbol SAVESTATE-HIT;
#X obj 200 1530 s screenLine2;
#X msg 20 1410 write -c /sdcard/phase8-probe.log;
#X obj 20 1610 text define \$0-log;
#X obj 640 1610 text define \$0-big;
#X text 20 1700 THE LOG APPEND IS u_err's \, TRAP AND ALL. text set wants a LIST \, and every line above arrives with its first word as the SELECTOR -- so list append is load-bearing and without it Pd answers no method for BOOT. text size gives the next line number and text set past the end APPENDS \, which is how the log grows with nothing tracking its length. Both measured in 0.49 rather than assumed -- see u_err.pd \, pd logfile., f 66;
#X text 660 1700 THE 2000 LINES ARE BUILT AT LOAD \, NOT AT SAVE. Building them is not part of the save path and must not be counted against the budget. What is timed is ONE text write of a text that already exists \, which is exactly what u_state will do. The Mac does this in 1.5 ms -- the SD card is the number that matters., f 60;
#X text 1400 620 S0-4 -- A RELATIVE WRITE \, no path at all \, so it lands in Pd's working directory. /tmp/patch is a SYMLINK to the patch folder on the SD card \, so if this appears in the patch folder WITHOUT a Save having copied it \, a relative write bypasses the whole /tmp/state mechanism., f 58;
#X text 1400 850 S0-2b -- KNOB 1 AT LOAD \, logged for the first three seconds only \, then the spigot closes so a streaming knob cannot fill the log. If a knobs.txt exists this is what mother pushes back from it. It also happens to answer item 68 -- whether mother STREAMS positions or sends only on movement -- which two phases have left open., f 58;
#X text 1400 1120 ONE TEXT DOES TWO JOBS. \$0-log is both the running log and the payload of the small write \, so probe-small.txt arrives with real content rather than being an empty marker -- which also proves the round trip carried BYTES and not just a filename., f 58;
